<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · text</p><h1 class="enc-title">Voting Rights Act of 1965</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1965</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Voting Rights Act of 1965 is a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a> law, signed by President Lyndon B. Johnson in August 1965 after the Selma to Montgomery marches, that prohibited racial discrimination in voting. It banned literacy tests and placed federal oversight on states with histories of discrimination, leading to a dramatic rise in Black voter registration in the South.</p></div>
